These are verbatim, LF pg_dump schema goldens from the tag named by prevRelease
in prev_release_columns_test.go. Old pods keep writing during rolling upgrades;
the integration tests compare these columns with the CURRENT migrated catalog
and replay frozen previous-release writers.

Refresh on EVERY release: edit prevRelease, regenerate the directory, re-freeze
the writer shapes from the tag. Run these Bash commands from the repository root
(after editing prevRelease to the previous released minor):

    release=$(sed -n 's/^const prevRelease = "\(.*\)"/\1/p' backend/tools/migrationdiff/prev_release_columns_test.go)
    test -n "$release" && git rev-parse --verify "refs/tags/$release" || exit 1
    fixtures=backend/tools/migrationdiff/testdata/prev-release
    find "$fixtures" -mindepth 1 -maxdepth 1 -type d -name 'v*' -exec rm -r -- {} +
    mkdir -p "$fixtures/$release"
    for f in $(git ls-tree -r --name-only "$release" backend/tools/migrationdiff/golden/); do
        git show "$release:$f" > "$fixtures/$release/$(basename "$f")" || exit 1
        cmp "$fixtures/$release/$(basename "$f")" <(git show "$release:$f") || exit 1
    done

Read the tagged sources, never substitute live models or embedded bases:

    git show "$release:backend/services/notification-management/model/model_state.go"
    git show "$release:backend/services/notification-management/model/api_state.go"
    git show "$release:backend/core/rdb/model.go"
    git show "$release:backend/services/device-state/model/model.go"
    git show "$release:backend/services/device-state/model/columnar_writes.go"
    git show "$release:backend/services/device-state/model/projection_merge.go"
    git show "$release:backend/services/device-state/model/dropped_measurements.go"
    git show "$release:backend/services/device-state/model/api.go"
    git show "$release:backend/services/device-state/model/ownership.go"
    git show "$release:backend/core/rdb/insert_columns.go"
    git show "$release:backend/core/rdb/insert_columns_upsert.go"
    git show "$release:backend/core/rdb/anchors.go"
    git diff --stat "$release" HEAD -- 'backend/services/*/schema/*' 'backend/services/*/model/migration*'

Expand the tagged bases by hand, preserving every field and gorm tag. Replay
every Create, full Save, distinct Updates/UpdateColumns map and delete shape,
including nullable values, and read back their effects. Cite each tagged function.
Regenerate the column-array SQL from the tagged column lists, conflict arms and
rdb builders; compare every frozen constant byte for byte. For gorm builders use
a Postgres DryRun with the service table prefix, including tenant callbacks (or
the equivalent explicit tenant predicates). Keep the column guard fail-loud and
the migration sync.Once.

    cd backend/tools/migrationdiff
    test -z "$(gofmt -l .)"
    go vet -tags integration ./...
    go build ./...
    go test -p 2 -count=1 ./...

Run the integration replays separately against Postgres.
